<title>GERMANY: Buba says German inflation remains &quot;very relaxed&quot;.</title>
<headline>Buba says German inflation remains &quot;very relaxed&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inflation in Germany has remained &quot;very relaxed&quot; despite higher world prices for crude oil and refined products in recent weeks, the Bundesbank said in a report on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The price environment in Germany remains up to now very relaxed,&quot; the German central bank said in its October report.</p>
<p>The Bundesbank noted that German import prices fell in August despite the price increase for energy.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
